[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit"]
[Variation "Declined, Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C30"]
[Character "gambit,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "d4-break,central-control"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 { Black ignores the pawn and aims at f2 instead. } 3. Nf3 { Develops a piece, covers h4 so ...Qh4+ is pointless, and attacks the pawn on e5. } 3... d6
4. c3 { Prepares d4: the c3 pawn supports it, so the bishop on c5 cannot win the centre pawn. [%cal Gc3d4] } 4... Nf6
5. d4 { Builds the centre. If Black takes, c3 recaptures with a strong pawn. } 5... exd4 6. cxd4 { Recaptures and attacks the bishop on c5, so White keeps a pawn in the centre. } 6... Bb6
7. Nc3 { Brings the knight out and adds pressure on e4 and d5. } 7... Nc6
8. Bb5 { Pins the knight on c6 to the king, so it cannot jump to d4 and White's centre stays safe. [%cal Gb5e8] } 8... O-O
9. O-O Bg4 10. Bxc6 { Removes the knight that eyes d4 and leaves Black with doubled pawns on the c-file. } 10... bxc6 *
